{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that describes a message one part of a program sends and other parts read later."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/event"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Event"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-Events","title":"Sending Events","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Events","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EventsView"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ReactingToChanges"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use events to decouple the code that notices something from the code that responds to it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a physics step sends a collision, and separate damage and sound systems each read it. Declare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an event as a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", send it with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/send(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and read it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/readEvents(_:by:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Collision: Event { var first: Entity, second: Entity }","enum DamageReader {}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Health(current: 3))","let asteroid = world.spawn(Health(current: 1))","world.send(Collision(first: ship, second: asteroid))","","for collision in world.readEvents(Collision.self, by: DamageReader.self) {","    world[Health.self, of: collision.first].current -= 1","}","print(world[Health.self, of: ship])","\/\/ Prints \"Health(current: 2)\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Events wait in the world’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Events","type":"reference"},{"text":" resource until ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/updateEvents()","type":"reference"},{"text":" drops them,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so senders and readers don’t need to run at the same moment. Unlike an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent","type":"reference"},{"text":", an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event isn’t aimed at an entity and runs no code when sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/RemovedComponent"],"title":"Conforming Types","type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Events.swift#L27","fileName":"Events.swift"},"externalID":"s:11WorldModule5EventP","role":"symbol","